  "transporter_equivariance_argument": {
    "argument": "The level-3 abelian cover construction is functorial for the basepoint-fixing mapping class action on V_K=H1(K;Q)/B. For any mapping-class word t carrying the base character chi0 to chi, the Fox-Jacobian chain map descends through d1 and the boundary subspace B to an isomorphism F_t:W_chi0->W_chi. For a stabilizer generator s of chi0, t s t^{-1} stabilizes chi and acts as F_t s F_t^{-1}. Thus the Hom equations for W_chi against the intrinsic rho_odd_theta_27 restriction are conjugate to the base Hom equations, preserving Hom dimension. The sector_728 transporter replay records transitivity on all 728 nonzero F_3 characters; therefore the base Hom-zero result propagates to every nonzero character.",
    "artifact": "tools/community-outreach/targets/problemsilike_04/sector_728_transporter_frontier_20260525_output.json",
